 The previous live asset package `dca354191bdeccc6562b6d191036da3bce9134dc0370c1294698e8730bb629ab`
 has one frozen, exact-version read-only layout snapshot to preserve its deployed
 historical presentation. It is not consulted for new revisions.
+
+## Source and review evidence boundaries
+
+New stage publication consumes `PublishRequest.content` JSON and its declared media; a new Markdown companion is not required. Retain the canonical Markdown and its original bytes for explicit legacy reading and historical comment anchors (`app.js` / `loadLegacyCase`). Do not delete legacy documents to simplify new publication.
+
+`source-binding.source_sha256` and `native_sha256` currently pass format validation only. That is not proof that either value equals the hash of the actual external source/native input bytes. The delivery producer must compute and compare those bytes separately and retain that evidence; the website has no such external input verification mechanism. Immutable media upload validation is separate from these two declarations.
+
+A package benchmark takes precedence. Unbound legacy packages retain the same-case registry preview already checked by `benchmarkSource`; bound packages without a benchmark show an explicit missing-source warning and never reuse the registry. Malformed declared metadata remains an error. No registry fallback proves the historical package's source/native hash.
+
+`GET /api/content` returns a default `approval: pending`, not a user approval receipt. Use authenticated `currentState` and exact-version `currentFeedback` from the feedback endpoint for review status; an unavailable state is unverified. Saved feedback is not an agent acceptance or processing receipt. No unattended pickup service is implemented by this contract.
